# Frontend task: Trimedixs customer selection

Build an attractive, usable English-language frontend for selecting a CRM customer for a fictional expense claim. Use only the public API https://crm-api.trimedixs.nl. Documentation: https://crm-api.trimedixs.nl/docs/. The complete OpenAPI contract is included below. You have no browser or tools; all required API information is supplied.

Return exactly one standalone HTML file with inline CSS and JavaScript. No frameworks, imports, external fonts, images, CDNs, installation, or build step. It opens from a local HTTP server and must also work on a static host. No backend, storage, authentication, API keys, invented write endpoints, or Supabase. All data is fictional. Keep customer selection in memory only.

Design a calm, professional interface for an expense app: a clear title, hierarchy, large click targets, good contrast, helpful English text, and a distinct selected-customer panel. Support desktop (1440 px), tablet (768 px), and mobile (375 px) without horizontal page overflow. Choose colors and layout yourself. Use semantic HTML, a visible input label, keyboard focus, aria-live status messages, native buttons, and a form that submits with Enter.

Functional contract and required HTML IDs:

1. Button id="check-connection" calls GET /api/v1/status. id="connection-status" explains whether the API is reachable and, on success, states that the data is fictional. Do not require automatic requests on page load. A simulated error from another endpoint must not mark the connection offline.
2. Form id="search-form" contains a visibly labeled input id="customer-search" and submit button id="search-button". Search company name or customer number, not city. Trim input; validate 2–100 characters before fetching. Empty, shorter, or longer input shows feedback without sending a search request. Do not silently truncate input. Both 2 and 100 characters are valid. Use exactly one correctly encoded search parameter through URLSearchParams, including for "Hart & Hand".
3. Show results in id="customer-results" with customerId, companyName, and city. Each result has a native selection button with data-customer-id="<customerId>". id="search-status" uses aria-live and distinguishes loading, success, and no matches. If total > limit, show the total and ask the user to refine the search; do not invent pagination.
4. Display the selected customer in id="selected-customer". Use data-field="customerId", data-field="companyName", and data-field="city" for exact field values rendered as text. A new selection replaces the old one. Button id="clear-selection" clears it. Clear selection immediately when starting a new search, even if that search fails or returns no results. Hide the panel or show a clear empty state when nothing is selected.
5. Button id="simulate-error" calls GET /api/v1/examples/error. Display the expected HTTP 503 and EXAMPLE_ERROR code in id="api-error". Also show the HTTP status and error code for HTTP 400 search errors in search-status or api-error. A subsequent valid search must recover; clear stale error messages as appropriate.
6. Catch network failures and apply an eight-second timeout per request, including reading JSON. Show understandable English network and timeout messages. Later actions must work again. Allow new searches while earlier requests are pending. Use cancellation or a sequence number to prevent stale responses and errors from overwriting newer results, status, or selection.
7. Render API fields as text, even when a company name contains markup such as <img src=x onerror=...>. Never execute API-supplied HTML. Send only GET requests, without credentials or a custom proxy. Show the URL and HTTP status of the latest active request in id="request-info" as a learning aid. Keep raw technical information secondary to the main controls.
8. Link to the Swagger documentation and OpenAPI JSON. Support keyboard-only use and narrow screens. Avoid loading-related layout shifts where practical.

Return only one complete HTML code block beginning with <!doctype html>. No explanation or second code block. Write the entire frontend yourself; there is no existing client implementation to copy.

Complete recorded OpenAPI contract:
{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "Trimedixs CRM-API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Read-only training API with 232 fictional healthcare organizations in the Netherlands. No authentication or HR data. Search for a customer and store its customerId and companyName with an expense claim in your own app. Unknown API routes return 404; write requests (POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE) return 405 with Allow: GET, OPTIONS. Errors use the Error schema. CORS allows cross-origin requests; do not send credentials."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "/",
      "description": "The API serving this documentation (local or deployed)"
    }
  ],
  "security": [],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Customers"
    },
    {
      "name": "Status"
    },
    {
      "name": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "name": "CORS"
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/api/v1/customers": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Customers"
        ],
        "operationId": "searchCustomers",
        "summary": "Search healthcare organizations by company name or customer ID",
        "description": "Case-insensitive search across 232 fictional healthcare organizations, matching companyName or customerId, not city. Provide search exactly once; leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed. Returns up to 20 matches ordered by customerId. Refine the search when total exceeds 20. Pagination is not supported.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "search",
            "in": "query",
            "required": true,
            "description": "Part of the company name or customer ID; 2–100 characters after trimming.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 2,
              "maxLength": 100
            },
            "examples": {
              "huisarts": {
                "value": "huisarts"
              },
              "customerId": {
                "value": "K-1001"
              },
              "specialCharacters": {
                "value": "Hart & Hand"
              },
              "noMatches": {
                "value": "bestaatniet"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Search results; no matches returns an empty customers array.",
            "headers": {
              "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "*"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "Cache-Control": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "no-store"
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SearchResult"
                },
                "example": {
                  "customers": [
                    {
                      "customerId": "K-1001",
                      "companyName": "Zorgcentrum Lindevaert",
                      "city": "Breda"
                    }
                  ],
                  "total": 1,
                  "limit": 20
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "The search parameter is missing, too short, too long or provided more than once.",
            "headers": {
              "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "*"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "Cache-Control": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "no-store"
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": {
                    "code": "INVALID_SEARCH",
                    "message": "Provide exactly one search parameter containing 2 to 100 characters."
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "tags": [
          "CORS"
        ],
        "operationId": "preflightSearchCustomers",
        "summary": "CORS preflight (performed by the browser)",
        "description": "Browsers send this request automatically when needed. You do not need to call it manually for a regular GET request.",
        "responses": {
          "204": {
            "description": "No content; the allowed methods and headers are returned.",
            "headers": {
              "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "*"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "Access-Control-Allow-Methods": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "example": "GET, OPTIONS"
                }
              },
              "Access-Control-Allow-Headers": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "example": "Accept, Content-Type"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/status": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Status"
        ],
        "operationId": "getStatus",
        "summary": "Check the API connection",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The API is available and the data is fictional.",
            "headers": {
              "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "*"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "Cache-Control": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "no-store"
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Status"
                },
                "example": {
                  "status": "ok",
                  "system": "Trimedixs CRM training API",
                  "version": "1",
                  "fictional": true
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "tags": [
          "CORS"
        ],
        "operationId": "preflightGetStatus",
        "summary": "CORS preflight (performed by the browser)",
        "description": "Browsers send this request automatically when needed. You do not need to call it manually for a regular GET request.",
        "responses": {
          "204": {
            "description": "No content; the allowed methods and headers are returned.",
            "headers": {
              "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "*"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "Access-Control-Allow-Methods": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "example": "GET, OPTIONS"
                }
              },
              "Access-Control-Allow-Headers": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "example": "Accept, Content-Type"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/examples/error": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Examples"
        ],
        "operationId": "getExampleError",
        "summary": "Practice error handling with an intentional 503 response",
        "description": "This endpoint always returns an error. The other endpoints remain available.",
        "responses": {
          "503": {
            "description": "Intentional example error; this does not mean the entire API is unavailable.",
            "headers": {
              "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "*"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "Cache-Control": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "no-store"
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": {
                    "code": "EXAMPLE_ERROR",
                    "message": "This is an intentional example error. Try the customer search endpoint next."
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "tags": [
          "CORS"
        ],
        "operationId": "preflightGetExampleError",
        "summary": "CORS preflight (performed by the browser)",
        "description": "Browsers send this request automatically when needed. You do not need to call it manually for a regular GET request.",
        "responses": {
          "204": {
            "description": "No content; the allowed methods and headers are returned.",
            "headers": {
              "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "*"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "Access-Control-Allow-Methods": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "example": "GET, OPTIONS"
                }
              },
              "Access-Control-Allow-Headers": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "example": "Accept, Content-Type"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": {
    "schemas": {
      "Customer": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "customerId",
          "companyName",
          "city"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "customerId": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^K-[0-9]{4}$",
            "example": "K-1001"
          },
          "companyName": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "Zorgcentrum Lindevaert"
          },
          "city": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "Breda"
          }
        }
      },
      "SearchResult": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "customers",
          "total",
          "limit"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "customers": {
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 20,
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Customer"
            }
          },
          "total": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "description": "The total number of matches, including those beyond the first 20 returned."
          },
          "limit": {
            "type": "integer",
            "enum": [
              20
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "Status": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "status",
          "system",
          "version",
          "fictional"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "status": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "ok"
            ]
          },
          "system": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "version": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "1"
            ]
          },
          "fictional": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "enum": [
              true
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "Error": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "error"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "error": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "required": [
              "code",
              "message"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "code": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "message": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
